in @optics/source/ganglion

# @optics/source/ganglion/abyss — gain medium for the abyss ganglion.
#
# Per docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §10.1, Fate's `abyss` ganglion
# performs depth-reading on holes via `@ai/abyss.depth(hole)` (per
# `boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror`). At the optical altitude, abyss
# is a 90-port diffractive surface (per §10.3, the D²NN identification
# of Lin et al. 2018); the source declaration here carries the active
# gain that drives the surface's transit during the kintsugi loop's
# ACTIVE pass (per §10.2).
#
# === Energy-balance declarations (per spec §3.9) ===
#
#   action       — `refract`. Per §10.3, phase-only diffractive
#                    transit (the D²NN layer's transmission pattern
#                    encodes weights; light refracts through the
#                    diffractive surface).
#   formalism    — `s_matrix`. Per §1.4 / §10.3, the 90×90
#                    multi-port topology requires the S-matrix
#                    formalism (the connectome's per-ganglion
#                    synaptic weights ARE the S-matrix).
#   energy       — `active`. Per §1.7, distinguishes source from
#                    passive facet.
#   pumping      — `io(channel: ref)`. Per §9.3 and recognition #57,
#                    energy injection IS the @io boundary crossing;
#                    the channel ref carries the @io binding (the
#                    user's prompt; the current substrate state; the
#                    recent metalogue session per §10.8).
#   gain_curve   — `ref` at @meta/ast. Per §4.9, the substrate-pull
#                    leaves the gain curve as @io's tick (a physical
#                    measurement, not a substrate computation).
#   sat          — `ref` at @meta/ast. Per §4.9, the saturation
#                    envelope discharges to @io.
#
# === The aperture refs (forward-promised) ===
#
# Input and output apertures are typed channels per §1.3. The
# `@optics/aperture/splinter` aperture carries the candidate envelope
# (Fate-emitted splinters as the beam's pre-bench state per §10.1);
# the `@optics/aperture/connectome` aperture carries the inter-
# ganglion handoff (the next-layer input of the 5-layer D²NN per
# §10.3). Both aperture declarations are forward-promised; this
# source declaration references them per the spec exemplar (§1.7
# uses forward-referenced `@optics/aperture/pump` and `@optics/
# aperture/coherent` in the same shape).
#
# === Why uniform with the other 4 ganglia at v1 ===
#
# Per `shards/optics/source/ganglion.mirror` header: v1 lands all 5
# ganglion sources with uniform shape; per-ganglion specialization
# (e.g., abyss might prefer a Lorentzian gain curve concentrated at
# the depth-reading eigenmode while explorer might prefer a flatter
# Gaussian for under-tried mode amplification) lands when the
# cascade's energy-balance opacity map surfaces the differentiation.
#
# === Recognition #58 Surface B closure ===
#
# This shard is one of 5 that close recognition #58's v1 gap (per
# Seam's adversarial review verdict). The other 4 sources land in
# sibling shards; together they discharge the
# `source_declares_energy_balance` property's requirement that the
# kintsugi loop's `oscillate.gain` MUST exist as an active source
# in the active-spectrometer bench (per §12.3, Brown 2003 cavity-
# enhanced reading).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.7 (source keyword
#               shape), §3.9 (energy-balance property), §10.1
#               (abyss IS depth-reading ganglion), §10.3 (D²NN
#               identification), §10.8 (Surface B).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]].
# Related shards: boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror (the ganglion
#                 type variant `abyss`),
#                 boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror
#                 (`@ai/abyss.depth(hole)`),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the resonator whose
#                 ACTIVE pass this source drives).

source @optics/source/ganglion/abyss {
  action:     refract,
  formalism:  s_matrix,
  energy:     active,
  pumping:    io(channel: ref),
  gain_curve: ref,
  sat:        ref,
  in:         aperture(@optics/aperture/splinter),
  out:        aperture(@optics/aperture/connectome),
}

out @optics/source/ganglion/abyss
